  "worked_solution": "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,7).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-8}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
